You can sort the array by id using the `sort` method and then reduce the array to count the ids. Here's a function that does that:

```typescript
function sortAndCountIds(items: { id: number }[]): number {
  return items.sort((a, b) => a.id - b.id).reduce((acc, curr) => acc + curr.id, 0);
}
```

This function first sorts the array by the `id` property and then reduces it to the sum of all `id` values.
